Vendored schemas and edition manifests
--------------------------------------

Fifteen files under spec/ are copied verbatim from the Vortex repository
(https://github.com/vortex-data/vortex) at tag 0.93.0, commit c1439e69bf, and
remain under its license. Upstream paths are the ones that tag uses.

    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright the Vortex contributors

    spec/flatbuffers/dtype.fbs    vortex-array/flatbuffers/vortex-dtype/dtype.fbs
    spec/flatbuffers/array.fbs    vortex-array/flatbuffers/vortex-array/array.fbs
    spec/flatbuffers/layout.fbs   vortex-layout/flatbuffers/vortex-layout/layout.fbs
    spec/flatbuffers/footer.fbs   vortex-file/flatbuffers/vortex-file/footer.fbs
    spec/proto/dtype.proto        vortex-array/proto/dtype.proto
    spec/proto/scalar.proto       vortex-array/proto/scalar.proto
    spec/proto/expr.proto         vortex-array/proto/expr.proto
    spec/editions/*.toml          vortex/editions/core/, the frozen core edition
                                  manifests, as upstream's xtask generates them

The three pages and the refresh script beside them are this repository's own.
spec/METADATA.md in particular is a transcription, not a copy: the per-encoding
metadata messages are Rust structs upstream, with no schema file to vendor.


